        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_013zygzMkSAxQ6m2NXyUmQTF",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022: \u0022concepts/single-composition-point.md\u0022, \u0022content\u0022: \u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Single Composition Point\\ndescription: Centralizing all scoped resource binding \u2014 credentials, paths, and configuration \u2014 at process startup ensures isolation, predictability, and auditability.\\ntimestamp: 2024-12-19T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - source-type/synthesis\\n  - concept/Single-Composition-Point\\n  - tech/dotnet\\nconfidence: high\\nconfidence_reason: \\\u0022Both source pages are authoritative architecture decisions describing complementary strategies that together form this pattern.\\\u0022\\nreview_date: 2025-06-19\\n---\\n\\n[[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] describe two independent architectural\\ndecisions that together form a unified pattern: **centralizing all resource binding and\\nconfiguration into a single composition point at process startup.**\\n\\n**Credential scoping** resolves the Anthropic API key in one place \u2014 before the child\\nprocess (Ingest or Query agent) starts \u2014 and injects it only into that child\u0027s isolated\\nenvironment. The Hub itself never holds the credential; the key exists only in the\\nshort-lived child process that actually uses it.\\n\\n**Runtime paths** resolves every file-system location \u2014 wiki content root, data\\ndirectory, database, secrets file, agent instructions \u2014 in one place at startup, before\\nany other part of the codebase needs them. No downstream code reads ambient working\\ndirectory or rediscovers paths on its own.\\n\\nTogether, these decisions establish that **all scoped resources \u2014 both secrets and\\nconfiguration \u2014 are bound exactly once, at the earliest possible moment, before any\\nagent or component runs.**\\n\\nThe benefits compound:\\n\\n- **Isolation**: Secrets never leak into a parent process\u0027s environment; paths are never\\n  accidentally inherited or misstated.\\n- **Predictability**: Every agent starts with the exact same view of what it has access\\n  to; there are no hidden dependencies or late bindings.\\n- **Auditability**: A single startup log shows all resource bindings; you can see\\n  exactly what each process was granted, and you can verify the source of each binding\\n  (command line, environment, config file, or default).\\n\\nThis pattern reduces the surface area for misconfigurations and the risk of scoping\\nerrors \u2014 the most common source of security and reliability problems in distributed\\nsystems. By binding all scoped resources at a single composition point, the system makes\\nit structurally harder to create agents with incorrect or incomplete credentials or\\npaths.\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
