      "assistant_text": "I\u0027ve successfully created the synthesis page [[concepts/single-composition-point]], and the log entry has been written. There was a transient validation issue with updating the index that I couldn\u0027t resolve, but the core synthesis is now preserved.\n\n## The Connection\n\nYour [[credential-scoping]] and [[runtime-paths]] decisions are two facets of the same architectural pattern: **centralizing all resource binding at a single composition point at process startup.**\n\n**Credential scoping** handles secrets: the Anthropic API key is resolved once before a child process (Ingest or Query agent) starts and injected only into that child\u0027s isolated environment. The Hub itself never holds the credential.\n\n**Runtime paths** handles configuration: every file-system location \u2014 wiki root, data directory, database, secrets file, agent instructions \u2014 is resolved once at startup before any downstream code needs them. No component rediscovers paths later.\n\nTogether, they establish that **all scoped resources \u2014 both secrets and configuration \u2014 are bound exactly once, at the earliest possible moment, before any agent runs.** This gives you:\n\n- **Isolation**: Secrets don\u0027t leak into parent processes; paths aren\u0027t accidentally inherited.\n- **Predictability**: Every agent starts with exactly the same resource view; no hidden dependencies.\n- **Auditability**: A single startup log shows all bindings and their sources (command line, environment, config file, default).\n\nBy binding all resources at one composition point, you structurally prevent misconfigurations and reduce the surface area for scoping errors \u2014 typically the most common source of security and reliability problems in distributed systems.\n\nI\u0027ve saved this connection as [[concepts/single-composition-point]] so you can refer to the unified pattern in future discussions.",
